{"id":"tropical-envelope","version":1,"category":"envelope","when":"Hot humid coastal or island contexts.","title":"Caribbean climate and envelope","combinations":"Pair shaded glazing with sheltered outdoor living and selective screening.","placement":"Place openings for potential cross ventilation and shelter entrances from driving rain; orientation and wind are assumptions until supplied.","principles":"Prioritize shade, weather protection and maintainable coastal materials; request local hurricane and corrosion engineering.","capabilities":"Screens, overhangs and openings can be constructed; no wind, corrosion, thermal or hurricane certification.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/designGuide.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Curated contextual application of the existing design guide; capability claims checked against scene/terra.ts and component-registry.ts."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["wall"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Screens, overhangs and openings can be constructed; no wind, corrosion, thermal or hurricane certification. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"outdoor-entertaining","version":1,"category":"programme","when":"Outdoor entertaining in a suitable climate or an explicit request.","title":"Outdoor kitchen, dining and bar","combinations":"Choose dining with kitchen or bar as appropriate; avoid installing every amenity.","placement":"Connect indoor kitchen, shaded dining and service route; separate heat and smoke from seating and bedrooms.","principles":"Make useful outdoor rooms with shade, furniture and circulation rather than empty decks.","capabilities":"Plates, screens, roofs, sofas and composed counter volumes supported; appliance assets, plumbing and smoke performance are not implemented.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/designGuide.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Curated contextual application of the existing design guide; capability claims checked against scene/terra.ts and component-registry.ts."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Plates, screens, roofs, sofas and composed counter volumes supported; appliance assets, plumbing and smoke performance are not implemented. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"legacy-recipe-65a14c7e-0559-45f0-adfe-589551ca499c","version":1,"category":"roof-outdoor","when":"Existing outdoor-living recipe; original compatible scales: mansion.","title":"Caribbean Hillside Dining Pavilion 02","combinations":"[{\"kind\":\"requires\",\"note\":\"within 10 m with direct service path\",\"target\":\"outdoor-kitchen\"},{\"kind\":\"requires\",\"note\":\"provide level, slip-resistant dining surface\",\"target\":\"patio\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"covering table and circulation edge\",\"target\":\"pergola\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"set above or beside pool with open ocean outlook\",\"target\":\"pool\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"layer warm overhead and pathway lighting\",\"target\":\"light\"},{\"kind\":\"conflicts\",\"note\":\"screen service and vehicle noise from dining area\",\"target\":\"driveway\"}]","placement":"Place on the ocean-facing side of the house with a level retained platform. Orient the long table parallel to the primary view rather than blocking it. Use a ventilated pergola with adjustable shade for tropical sun and brief rain. Keep the kitchen service route direct, step-free, and visually discreet. Protect the uphill edge from gusts using louvers or layered tropical planting. Maintain an unobstructed circulation band around the table and toward the view edge.","principles":"Adapt approved guidance to the brief. Parameter options: [{\"key\":\"diningAreaWidth\",\"max\":14,\"min\":5,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":8},{\"key\":\"diningAreaDepth\",\"max\":10,\"min\":4,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":6},{\"key\":\"tableSeatCount\",\"max\":20,\"min\":8,\"unit\":\"count\",\"value\":12},{\"key\":\"pergolaCoverage\",\"max\":90,\"min\":35,\"unit\":\"%\",\"value\":65},{\"key\":\"viewEdgeClearance\",\"max\":5,\"min\":1.5,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":2.5},{\"key\":\"kitchenDistance\",\"max\":10,\"min\":2,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":5},{\"key\":\"ambientLightingLevel\",\"max\":150,\"min\":30,\"unit\":\"lux\",\"value\":80},{\"key\":\"windScreenType\",\"unit\":\"string\",\"value\":\"timber-louver\",\"options\":[\"none\",\"planting\",\"timber-louver\",\"glass-screen\"]}].","capabilities":"Required capabilities: . Check against the scene construction contract; approval does not implement capabilities.","sources":[{"reference":"library recipe 65a14c7e-0559-45f0-adfe-589551ca499c","note":"Existing recipe approval; no new external verification.","kind":"repository","verified":false}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Required capabilities: . Check against the scene construction contract; approval does not implement capabilities. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"estate-composition","version":1,"category":"composition","when":"Large private residences with substantial entertaining and service needs.","title":"Estate programme and hierarchy","combinations":"Consider guest accommodation and wellness only after a complete main residence.","placement":"Sequence arrival, entrance, living, shaded terrace and view; separate service access and private suites.","principles":"Give secondary volumes a programme and subordinate them to the residence.","capabilities":"Compose plates, walls, openings and roofs freely; no prescribed wing arrangement.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/designGuide.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Curated contextual application of the existing design guide; capability claims checked against scene/terra.ts and component-registry.ts."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Compose plates, walls, openings and roofs freely; no prescribed wing arrangement. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"tropical-contemporary","version":1,"category":"climate-site","when":"Warm climate residence combining openness and shelter.","title":"Tropical contemporary character","combinations":"Vary roof forms with programme.","placement":"Compose deep roofs, shaded glazing, stone bases and timber screens around outdoor rooms.","principles":"Avoid a glass box with decorative palms as the only climate response.","capabilities":"roof, walls, glazing, screens and volume detail; landscape assets and climate performance not certified.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Operation availability checked against the direct-scene contract. Design guidance is conceptual curation, not a verified regulation or external research."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"roof, walls, glazing, screens and volume detail; landscape assets and climate performance not certified. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"covered-threshold","version":1,"category":"arrival","when":"Weather protection at the front door.","title":"Covered entrance threshold","combinations":"Choose wall returns or posts.","placement":"Connect approach slab to a recessed door under a supported canopy.","principles":"Avoid a door behind an uncut wall.","capabilities":"plate, unglazed wall opening, entrance child, volume posts and roof.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Operation availability checked against the direct-scene contract. Design guidance is conceptual curation, not a verified regulation or external research."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","entrance","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"plate, unglazed wall opening, entrance child, volume posts and roof. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"facade-materials","version":1,"category":"materials","when":"A residence needing coherent enclosure and material expression.","title":"Facade depth, roofs and material identity","combinations":"Coordinate a small material palette, roof edges, recessed entrances and shaded openings.","placement":"Relate facade rhythm to rooms and privacy; carry architectural intent around side and rear elevations.","principles":"Adapt material and roof recommendations to climate and style instead of prescribing a fixed house template.","capabilities":"Existing ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage; flat, gable and hip roofs; curved roof only via approved open pavilion.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/designGuide.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Curated contextual application of the existing design guide; capability claims checked against scene/terra.ts and component-registry.ts."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["wall"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Existing ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage; flat, gable and hip roofs; curved roof only via approved open pavilion. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"court-water-separation","version":1,"category":"roof-outdoor","when":"Use when the brief or chosen programme calls for court water and walking route.","title":"Court water and walking route","combinations":"Timber shade members and limestone outdoor paving; ivory supports keep a quiet background.","placement":"If water is requested separate its basin from a continuous dry circulation edge.","principles":"Do not use a water plane as pedestrian circulation.","capabilities":"Use direct-scene primitives: plate, roof, volume. No planting generator, curved pergolas, rain drainage or microclimate simulation.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Checked primitive names against the direct-scene contract; individually curated conceptual relationships, not external research or a regulation."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","roof","volume"],"materials":"Timber shade members and limestone outdoor paving; ivory supports keep a quiet background.","supports":"Construct connected walking plates with explicit shade supports and actual room thresholds nearby.","unsupported":"No planting generator, curved pergolas, rain drainage or microclimate simulation."}}
{"id":"composition-hierarchy","version":1,"category":"composition","when":"Large programmes needing a legible centre.","title":"Primary and subordinate massing","combinations":"Compare arrival and garden silhouettes.","placement":"Give the principal living hall the strongest volume; step bedroom and service wings down around it.","principles":"Avoid equal boxes with no hierarchy.","capabilities":"plate, wall, roof and volume; compose hollow rooms, not solid habitable blocks.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Operation availability checked against the direct-scene contract. Design guidance is conceptual curation, not a verified regulation or external research."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"plate, wall, roof and volume; compose hollow rooms, not solid habitable blocks. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"hip-shelter","version":1,"category":"roof-outdoor","when":"Four sided shelter over a rectangular volume.","title":"Hip roof shelter","combinations":"Use subordinate hips or flat links.","placement":"Set eaves above enclosure and coordinate veranda canopies below main eaves.","principles":"Avoid claiming arbitrary roof polygons.","capabilities":"roofForm hip and overhang on rectangular footprint; flashing and hurricane uplift need engineering.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Operation availability checked against the direct-scene contract. Design guidance is conceptual curation, not a verified regulation or external research."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"roofForm hip and overhang on rectangular footprint; flashing and hurricane uplift need engineering. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
